            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis is not planned at the moment due to either high complexity or needing to introduce third party dependency. Plus, it doesn't really fit the [decision of not trying to be a full file explorer](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4228f166ee9db3e910eea1915e2d3683028add47/doc/mini-files.txt#L26-L28): as it is not reasonable to expect images to be edited, having they anything extra is (currently) out of scope.\r\n\r\nClosing as \"currently it is too complex to support; once there is built-in tools in Neovim itself for that (see neovim/neovim#30889), this can be revisited\".",
